# clang-format style for the installer C sources (installer/src).
#
# Mirrors the codebase's existing conventions as closely as clang-format can:
# 4-space indent, K&R braces, pointers glued to the name (`int *x`), single-line
# if/loop/switch-case statements kept on one line, 2 spaces before trailing
# comments, no forced column wrapping (ColumnLimit 0 — the code knowingly uses
# long lines for snprintf chains and macros).
#
# Deliberate deviations the formatter enforces (one-time churn on adoption):
#   - preprocessor directives are NOT indented (IndentPPDirectives: None)
#   - multi-statement one-line blocks `if (x) { a; b; }` are split (this clang
#     version only keeps <2 statements on one line under ColumnLimit: 0)
#   - macros are re-laid-out (clang-format always breaks do{...}while macros)
#   - trailing `/* */` comments drop to one space (SpacesBeforeTrailingComments
#     only applies to `//` comments here)
#
# Clang-format cannot express the hand-written 2-space preprocessor-directive
# indent or the aligned `#define NAME   value` columns; both were dropped in
# favor of the formatter's canonical output.
#
# Run via `pnpm format:c` / `pnpm lint:c` (see tools/format-c.mjs).
BasedOnStyle: LLVM
IndentWidth: 4
TabWidth: 4
ColumnLimit: 0
PointerAlignment: Right
SortIncludes: false
AllowShortLoopsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortIfStatementsOnASingleLine: Always
AllowShortCaseLabelsOnASingleLine: true
AllowShortBlocksOnASingleLine: Always
IndentCaseLabels: true
SpacesBeforeTrailingComments: 2
Cpp11BracedListStyle: false